    Bug 2027513 - Create <lazy-findbar> custom element to prevent premature Finder binding and fix stale match counts. r=freaktechnik

    Bug 2016950 changed the prototype document sink to use FROM_PARSER_NETWORK
    for HTML Custom Elements. For statically stamped findbars in windows that
    undergo remoteness changes (like aboutMessage and viewSource), this parser
    delay caused the findbar to prematurely bind to the browser's initial
    Finder instance. When the browser later swapped its frame loader, the
    Finder instance was orphaned, causing the findbar to miss
    onMatchesCountResult callbacks.

    To resolve this, this patch introduces a new `<lazy-findbar>` wrapper
    custom element extending HTMLElement. This wrapper acts as a pure, transparent
    proxy (`display: contents`), intercepting passive state checks (`hidden`,
    `clear`) without DOM manipulation, and only instantiates the true XUL
    `<findbar>` when an active search command is executed.

    By replacing the static tags in aboutMessage, viewSource, and
    chat-messenger with `<html:lazy-findbar>`, it bypasses the parser delay and
    safely attaches to the final, stable Finder. For the Chat window,
    deferring initialization prevents the background findbar from attaching
    to the global "Highlight All" preference observer, resolving a long-standing
    bug where toggling the preference caused a "controller is null" crash in
    hidden chat logs.

    Furthermore, this patch unifies the 3-pane findbar architecture by
    replacing imperative DOM creation in `message-pane.mjs` with statically
    stamped `<lazy-findbar>` tags in the message pane template. Because
    the wrapper intercepts passive `.close()` and `.clear()` calls during
    tab switching, the 3-pane startup cycle remains completely zero-cost.

    Finally, this patch resolves an IPC race condition in msgHdrView.js.
    When switching messages with the findbar open, yielding to the event loop
    allows the async Finder teardown of the previous message to complete
    cleanly before a new search is initiated, preventing overlapping and
    stale match counts.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D293383

